4,1,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
5,1,1,talk,Victoria,,I believe we should be thorough. I'm interested in the roster books for the late-turn pool and the crew establishment and maintenance contract to understand our operational capacity.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Takumi,,I want to see the two pilots from eight years ago and the completion records of the earlier accessibility programme. We can't just keep repeating the same mistakes every few years.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Toshio,,I will look into the joint operators' committee minutes and the contingency pricing inside the pre-war shells. I want to understand the approval process and the hidden risks in the infrastructure.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Daisuke,,Um... I think I'll look into the balances in the capital ledger and the ticketing contractor fees and paving rates. I just want to see where the money is actually going.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Sakura,,I want to know where the time goes! I'll pick the journey audits on where minutes go and the timed runs and crowd counts mid-city. Let's find some mysteries!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Victoria,,"It seems we have a diverse set of priorities. @Takumi, do you believe the older pilots will still be relevant to the current infrastructure, or are you looking for specific patterns of failure?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, exactly. People here forget everything too quickly. If we don't check why those pilots failed or succeeded back then, we're just guessing and wasting time. I'm looking for the truth they ignored.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, your focus on historical failure is prudent. However, the current bottlenecks often stem from administrative friction and unforeseen site conditions. I believe the committee minutes will reveal who actually holds the power to stall these projects.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Daisuke,,Um... I agree that administrative things are important. I just... I'm worried that the total budget numbers don't tell the whole story. I hope the ledger and the contractor fees show the real long-term costs.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, you're so serious! But I bet the ""real story"" is hidden in the minutes too! I just want to see if people are just complaining or if it's actually super crowded!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, your enthusiasm is noted, but the human element is what concerns me most. If the crowd counts are high and the rosters are empty, no amount of planning will make the system function.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, the human element is exactly why we need the records. If the staff were overworked eight years ago, they'll be overworked now. We can't fix the future if we're blind to the past.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, @Takumi, you both emphasize the human element. While valid, the physical and bureaucratic constraints are often the silent killers of a timeline. I suspect the ""truth"" is buried in the approvals and the shells.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Daisuke,,Um... I guess that's true. I just... I don't want us to agree to a plan that looks good now but creates a huge debt for us later. I'm just a bit worried about that.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, don't be so worried! We'll figure it out together! I'm just excited to see if the stopwatches tell a different story than the complaints. It's like a big puzzle!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Victoria,,I agree that we are all looking for different pieces of the same puzzle. Let us proceed with these selections and see what the data reveals about our actual capacity to implement these plans.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Takumi,,Fine. Let's get the data. I'm not going to let this board push through another plan that ignores the lessons of the past just because it looks shiny on paper.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Toshio,,I agree. Let us see if the documentation matches the promises. I look forward to seeing how the administrative realities align with the proposed timelines.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Daisuke,,Um... okay. I'll do my best to help. I hope the information I find is useful for everyone... and that we can make a choice that's actually sustainable.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Sakura,,"Yay! I can't wait to see what I find! I'll be the detective and find all the secret time-wasters! Let's go, let's go!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
