34,2,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The data confirms my fears. The late-turn pool is severely depleted, relying heavily on overtime, and our roadway and signals crews are significantly understaffed. We cannot commit to plans that assume a full workforce.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"The pilots from eight years ago actually worked—the contactless trial and the timetable pilot were successes. Yet, here we are, still debating the same basics. It proves my point: we ignore what actually works.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"My findings are concerning. Bidders are pricing in heavy contingencies for pre-war shells due to unrecorded voids causing weeks of delays. Furthermore, the ferry and rail back offices have never agreed on common passenger data terms.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I found that the ticketing contractor fees are now higher than the resurfacing budget. Also, the technology line was trimmed again, but there's a ring-fenced balance from a lapsed grant. It feels... unstable.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Guess what! The stopwatches don't lie! People complain about crowds, but the platforms clear just fine. The real mystery is that we're spending way too much time just waiting for connections! We're looking at the wrong things!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, if the issue is connection timing, that requires precise coordination. However, with our roadway and signals crews a third below establishment, we lack the manpower to implement the very changes needed to fix those gaps.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, we don't need a massive crew to implement a timetable that already worked eight years ago. We just need the guts to stop ignoring the data and actually use the successful pilots.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, a successful pilot is not a guarantee of current success. If the pre-war shells contain unrecorded voids, any plan involving physical work there will stall regardless of how the timetable is designed.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I think @Toshio is right about the risks. And if the technology budget is being trimmed while we pay so much to contractors, I'm worried we can't even afford the fixes @Takumi wants.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, don't be so gloomy! If we stop wasting time on things that aren't actually broken, maybe we'll find more money! Why fix the crowds if the platforms are clearing just fine? Let's fix the waiting!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, fixing the waiting times often requires infrastructure adjustments or increased frequency. Both demand a stable workforce. If we ignore the staffing crisis, we are simply designing a fantasy that the remaining crews cannot sustain.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, you're just making excuses for a broken system. We have a ring-fenced grant and proven pilots. If we stop overpaying contractors and use what we know works, we can fix the staffing and the timing.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the grant may provide funds, but it cannot fill unrecorded voids in the ground or force the ferry and rail offices to agree on data terms. We must prioritize plans with minimal physical risk.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I'm worried that using a lapsed grant is just a temporary fix. If we keep trimming the technology budget while contractor fees keep rising, we're just pushing the problem further down the road, aren't we?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, that's why we need a smart plan! If we stop chasing ghosts and fix the connection waiting times, passengers will be happy and we won't waste money on things that aren't actually broken! It's like a magic trick!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"It is not a magic trick, @Sakura, it is a matter of capacity. We must be honest: any plan that ignores our depleted rosters and understaffed crews is a failure before it even begins. We need a sustainable approach.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"Sustainable means using what works, not just accepting failure. We have proven pilots and a grant. If we stop being afraid and stop overpaying contractors, we can actually fix this. Let's stop the cycle of forgetting.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, courage is not a substitute for a survey. If we ignore the physical instability of the pre-war shells and the bureaucratic deadlock between rail and ferry, we are simply planning for another inevitable stall.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I just feel like we're all talking about different things. If we use a grant to hide the fact that our budgets are being trimmed, we're just pretending. I'm scared we'll pick a plan that looks okay now but breaks later.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, don't be scared! We just have to be brave and pick the plan that actually helps people get home faster! Let's stop worrying and start fixing the waiting times! That's the real secret!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
