58,3,,status,Sakura,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Given the severe depletion of the late-turn pool and the staffing shortage in roadway and signals crews, Plan B is an impossibility. We cannot extend hours when our current rosters are already failing.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, you're still thinking in terms of failure. Plan B is exactly what the pilot eight years ago proved was possible and cost-effective. We have the data; we just need the will to implement it.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, will is irrelevant when the ground is unstable. Plan C is a disaster waiting to happen; those pre-war shells will lead to the same unrecorded voids and weeks of delays we've seen recently.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I'm really worried about Plan D. If we're already paying too much to three different ticketing contractors and the technology budget is being trimmed, can we actually afford a new platform without more debt?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, don't be a worry-wart! Plan A is the best! It fixes the mid-city surface route where the timed runs were slow, and it helps people get across the city faster without waiting! Let's do it!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, Plan A requires rebuilding boarding islands and dedicated lanes, which relies on the roadway crews that are currently a third below establishment. We cannot ignore the fact that we lack the manpower for major construction.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, you're just blocking everything! If we can't do construction, then Plan B is the only logical choice. It's a timetable and roster shift—something we already proved works. Stop letting the current mess stop us from fixing it.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, Plan B ignores the staffing crisis @Victoria highlighted. However, Plan D is equally flawed; the ferry and rail offices cannot even agree on data terms. We cannot integrate fares if the operators cannot agree on the data.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... if Plan D is a deadlock and Plan C is too risky, maybe Plan A is better? But @Victoria is right about the crews... I just don't want a plan that creates more debt.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Victoria, we can just be super efficient! Plan A fixes the slow parts I found with my stopwatch! If we don't fix the mid-city route, people will just keep waiting and waiting. That's the real problem!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, efficiency cannot replace missing people. @Takumi, a pilot from eight years ago does not magically refill today's depleted rosters. If we must choose, we need the plan with the lowest operational and physical risk.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, the lowest risk is doing nothing, and that's how we got here! Plan B is a proven success. If we use the ring-fenced grant @Daisuke found, we can actually afford to fix the staffing.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, a grant cannot conjure staff from thin air. Plan B is a fantasy. Plan A is the only option that avoids the bureaucratic deadlock of Plan D and the physical hazards of Plan C.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... if @Toshio thinks Plan A is the safest, maybe it's the right choice? I'm still worried about the costs, but it seems less likely to fail completely than the others. I'll try to agree.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Sakura,,Yay! See? Everyone is starting to agree! Plan A is the winner because it fixes the slow parts and gets people moving! Let's stop the waiting and start the zooming! I vote for Plan A!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"I still have grave concerns about the roadway crews, but compared to the staffing impossibility of Plan B, the physical risks of Plan C, and the deadlock of Plan D, Plan A is the most viable. I vote for Plan A.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"I'm not happy about giving up on a proven success like Plan B, but I won't let us get stuck in a deadlock. If we're doing Plan A, we'd better actually finish it. I vote for Plan A.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"Plan A avoids the structural voids of the shells and the data deadlock between operators. While staffing is a concern, it is the only plan not fundamentally doomed by hidden risks. I vote for Plan A.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I'm still a bit nervous about the budget and the crews, but since everyone else agrees and it seems the least risky, I'll go along with it. I vote for Plan A.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Sakura,,I'm so happy we all agree! Let's make the city zoom and get rid of those boring waiting times! I vote for Plan A!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
